{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.632 acc, a large jump over singleprofile configs (~0.53). In singleprofile, pca_n2000 and scvi_n200 performed similarly (0.527 vs 0.536), but it is unclear whether this equivalence holds under multiprofile+avgpool, where the learned non-linear representation from scvi may interact differently with cross-profile pooling than a linear PCA embedding. Question: Does the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000) materially affect performance when multiprofile+avgpool aggregation is active? config_003 changes only the RNA encoder from config_002, isolating this variable. Why best next: It is the cleanest single-variable comparison to the current best, and the answer directly determines whether we can simplify the RNA pipeline (pca_n2000 is cheaper and more interpretable) or must retain scvi_n200, which constrains all subsequent multiprofile experiments. Under a limited budget, resolving whether the encoder choice is a free parameter or a critical one is more informative than testing fusion or image-encoder variations, which are secondary to the representation question."
}

